-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The moments an [Auto] or a [Counter] answers to (manual 9-6), as the events
-- that *are* them.
--
-- A trigger is a name in the legacy engine, matched against the event log by
-- TypeScript. Here it is an event pattern, so a game can declare its own
-- moments without code — and so the engine's moments can be read against the
-- manual rather than against `pendTriggers`.
--
-- Four conventions hold across the file.
--
--   ON <event>(field: value, …)
--     The event and the fields that have to match. Event names are the
--     definition's own; which of them a game fires is Stage 4's business.
--     Only `from`, `to`, `in`, `area` and `zone` name a DEFINE ZONE and are
--     checked by the loader — every other argument is a word about the event
--     itself, so `attackDeclared(target: leader)` is a part in the attack and
--     not a place.
--
--   watcher: controller | opponent | both | fromHolder
--     Whose cards in play are asked, when the moment is not the answering
--     card's own. `controller` is the side the event is about (the moved
--     card's master, the damaged player); `opponent` is the other one.
--     `fromHolder` is the original area holder carried by a movement.
--     Left out, only the card the event is about answers.
--
--   WHERE
--     A condition on the answering side rather than on the event.
--     `isTurnPlayer(who: you)` is what "your Charge Phase" means on a card,
--     and "your opponent's turn" is the same condition from the other chair
--     (7-1) — never a duration.
--
--   BIND
--     What the event's card is called inside the program: "self" when the
--     moment happened to the answering card, "subject" when it happened to
--     another card that the answering card is watching. A watcher list that
--     includes the card itself (a Unison paying its own [Spirit Boost], a
--     Life card turned face up) binds "subject" all the same — there it is
--     the same card.
--
-- The names are the `Trigger` union's, and `text:` is the record's WHEN in
-- words, so `scripts/verify/rulesets.ts` can hold the two to one list.
-- The five `counter:*` declarations at the foot are the counter windows
-- (4-3, 9-7): the moments a [Counter] answers to rather than an [Auto], and
-- the only names here a card's WHEN never says.
-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- ── playing and placing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- §6-2-4 — when your Leader is placed
DEFINE TRIGGER leaderPlaced
  ON moved(to: leader)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when your Leader is placed"

-- §9-6-9-4 — when this card is played
DEFINE TRIGGER played
  ON moved(asPlay: true, to: [battle, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is played"

-- §9-6-9-4 — when this card is played from your hand (#936): the same
-- arrival, asking where the card was when it was played. `from` is the
-- origin captured by the move itself (a normal play, or a skill's play from
-- the hand), never the zone after entry or the source skill's text.
DEFINE TRIGGER playedFromHand
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: hand, to: [battle, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is played from your hand"

-- Audit triggers 1 — when this card is played from the Drop (TB3-039, "When you
-- play this card from a Drop Area"): the same arrival as `playedFromHand`, asking
-- for the Drop as the origin the move captured.
DEFINE TRIGGER playedFromDrop
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: drop, to: [battle, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is played from your Drop"

-- §22-15 — when this card is played using [Over Realm]: the same arrival,
-- made by [Over Realm]'s own move, which says so on its `play` (`using:` in
-- keywords.rules). An ordinary play carries no `using`, so it never matches.
DEFINE TRIGGER playedUsingOverRealm
  ON moved(asPlay: true, to: battle, using: "Over Realm")
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is played using [Over Realm]"

-- §5-5 — when you play a card
DEFINE TRIGGER youPlayed
  ON moved(asPlay: true, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you play a card"

-- §5-5 — when your opponent plays a card
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentPlayed
  ON moved(asPlay: true, to: [battle, unison], watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent plays a card"

-- #1015 — when your opponent uses a skill to play a card (BT15-005, BT15-085,
-- BT15-101, BT12-132): the play is the opponent's own skill's (`by: skill`,
-- `byOpponent: false` — the cause is not the other player's), never a play the
-- opponent declared from their hand. `opponentPlayed` above is any arrival.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentPlayedBySkill
  ON moved(asPlay: true, by: skill, byOpponent: false, to: [battle, unison], watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent uses a skill to play a card"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When one of your opponent's Battle Cards is played by a
-- skill" (BT21-105): any skill, either player's — `opponentPlayedBySkill` is
-- their own.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardPlayedBySkill
  ON moved(asPlay: true, by: skill, to: [battle, unison], watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your opponent's cards is played by a skill"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — another card of yours played from a place the card names:
-- "When {Destined Conclusion Piccolo Jr.} is played from your hand" (TB2-045),
-- "When a <Son Goku: GT> card is played from your Drop" (BT26-001b). The card
-- played is the subject; what the text says about it is a condition on it.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPlayedFromHand
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: hand, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is played from your hand"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPlayedFromDrop
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: drop, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is played from your Drop"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When your or your opponent's <Majin Buu> card is played"
-- (BT28-100): a play on either side of the table.
DEFINE TRIGGER eitherCardPlayed
  ON moved(asPlay: true, to: [battle, unison], watcher: both)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card is played by either player"

-- #1163 — when your card is played by this card's skill (BT29-083): your own
-- skill's play (`by: skill, byOpponent: false`), and only the one the watching
-- card's own skill made — `byWatcher: true` asks that the card whose skill
-- played it is the card being asked, which no other moment says.
DEFINE TRIGGER youPlayedByThisCard
  ON moved(asPlay: true, by: skill, byOpponent: false, byWatcher: true, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your card is played by this card's skill"

-- §5-5-4 — when this card is placed in a Battle Area. 5-5-1: playing a card
-- places it in the Battle Area, so a play is one of the ways this happens and
-- the pattern does not ask `asPlay` (owner's ruling, 2 Oct 2026). A skill whose
-- record also says `played` answers the one arrival once (`vm/triggers.ts`).
DEFINE TRIGGER placed
  ON moved(to: battle)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is placed in a Battle Area"

-- §5-5-4 — when a card is placed in your Battle Area: the same arrival,
-- watched by the cards of the side whose Battle Area it arrived in. Played or
-- placed by a skill alike (5-5-1, owner's ruling of 2 Oct 2026). The card is
-- the subject, and what the card says about it ("a {Scouter}", "one of your
-- blue Z-Extras", BT23-066, BT22-032b) is a condition on that subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPlaced
  ON moved(to: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card is placed in your Battle Area"

-- ── battles (8-1 … 8-5) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- §8-1-3 — when this card attacks
DEFINE TRIGGER attacks
  ON attackDeclared(role: attacker)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card attacks"

-- §8-1-3 — when this card is attacked
DEFINE TRIGGER attacked
  ON attackDeclared(role: target)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is attacked"

-- §8-1-3 — when your opponent attacks
--
-- `role: attacker` is #150's addition, the first stage to actually fire an
-- `attackDeclared` moment: a battle names two cards, the attacker and the
-- guard, and `vm/battle.ts` fires one moment for each so `attacks`/`attacked`
-- can each `BIND "self"` to the right one. Without a role narrowing this
-- pattern, the *guard's* own moment would match it too (its `watcher:
-- opponent` asks nothing about which card the moment is about, only who is
-- asked), which would pend this trigger a second time off the wrong subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentAttacks
  ON attackDeclared(role: attacker, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent attacks"

-- §8-1-3 — when a Battle Card attacks (BT8-089, prohibition batch 5): any
-- player's Battle Card, watched by every player's cards in play. The attacker's
-- own moment (`role: attacker`) marks a Battle Card attacking from the Battle
-- Area (`battleCard: true`, 8-1-1); a Leader's or a Unison's attack is not it.
DEFINE TRIGGER battleCardAttacks
  ON attackDeclared(role: attacker, battleCard: true, watcher: both)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a Battle Card attacks"

-- §5-5-4 — when a player places a card in a Battle Area (BT15-091,
-- prohibition batch 6): either player's card arriving in any Battle Area,
-- played or placed by a skill alike (5-5-1), watched by every player's cards
-- in play. What the card says about it ("a [Field] Extra Card") is a condition
-- on the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER aPlayerPlacesInBattle
  ON moved(to: battle, watcher: both)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a player places a card in a Battle Area"

-- §3-1-5 — when a player's card leaves a Battle Area (BT15-091's back): either
-- player's card, to any area, by any cause, read as it was when it left.
DEFINE TRIGGER aPlayersCardLeftBattle
  ON moved(from: battle, watcher: both)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a player's card leaves a Battle Area"

-- Phrasing batch 5 — when one of your cards attacks: "When your ≪Saiyan≫ card
-- attacks" (BT27-001), "When your Battle Cards attack" (BT2-003). The attacking
-- card is the subject; what the card says about it is a condition on it.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardAttacks
  ON attackDeclared(role: attacker, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards attacks"

-- SD15-01 — when the opponent attacks the specific red Unison named by the
-- card. The target declaration is a separate role from the attacking card;
-- its current attributes are carried on that target moment, while the Auto
-- remains on the controller's board and BINDs self.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentAttacksRedUnison2
  ON attackDeclared(role: target, target: unison, initial: true, targetRed: true, targetSpecifiedCost: 2, watcher: controller)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when your opponent attacks your red Unison Card with a specified cost of 2"

-- §8-1-3 — when your Leader is attacked
DEFINE TRIGGER yourLeaderAttacked
  ON attackDeclared(target: leader, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your Leader is attacked"

-- §8-2 — at the start of the offense step
DEFINE TRIGGER offenseStart
  ON stepStart(step: offense)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: you)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of the offense step"

-- §8-3 — at the start of the defense step
DEFINE TRIGGER defenseStart
  ON stepStart(step: defense)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: opponent)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of the defense step"

-- §8-4 — at the start of the damage step
DEFINE TRIGGER damageStart
  ON stepStart(step: damage, watcher: both)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of the damage step"

-- §8-5 — at the end of the battle
DEFINE TRIGGER battleEnd
  ON stepStart(step: battleEnd, watcher: both)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the end of the battle"

-- ── KOs (5-12, 21-14) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- §5-12 — when this card is KO'd
--
-- `role: koed` is #150's addition, for the same reason `opponentAttacks`
-- above needed one: a KO names two cards, the one that left and the one that
-- caused it (`kos`, `role: cause`, already declared), and `vm/battle.ts`
-- fires one `ko` moment for each. Left bare, this pattern's empty `ON ko`
-- would match *either* moment — the koed card's own and the attacker's —
-- since a pattern with no arguments is true of any event carrying that name;
-- naming the koed card's own role is what keeps it from also asking the
-- attacker "were you KO'd". `to: drop` is 9-1-3-1's derived exception,
-- exactly as `droppedFromBattle` below reads it for a skill's own move: a
-- card asking whether it was just KO'd is asked about its own departure
-- *after* it has already landed in the Drop, so the pattern has to name the
-- place its skills are still valid in reacting to, the same as any other
-- "fires while the card is elsewhere" moment.
DEFINE TRIGGER koed
  ON ko(role: koed, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is KO'd"

-- Audit triggers 1 — this card KO'd and how: "…KO'd by an opponent's attack"
-- (EX21-05, BT15-071; a battle's KO, 8-4-6-2), "…KO'd by your opponent" (BT15-006;
-- their attack or their skill), "…KO'd by an opponent's skill" (BT20-078), "…by
-- one of your skills" (BT23-039), "…by a <Vegeta> card's skill" (BT25-051; any
-- skill, the card that KO'd it the subject the compiler asks). Plain `koed` above
-- is every KO.
DEFINE TRIGGER koedByAttack
  ON ko(role: koed, to: drop, by: battle)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is KO'd by an attack"

DEFINE TRIGGER koedByOpponent
  ON ko(role: koed, to: drop, byOpponent: true)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is KO'd by your opponent"

DEFINE TRIGGER koedBySkill
  ON ko(role: koed, to: drop, by: skill)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is KO'd by a skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER koedByYourSkill
  ON ko(role: koed, to: drop, by: skill, byOpponent: false)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is KO'd by one of your skills"

DEFINE TRIGGER koedByOpponentSkill
  ON ko(role: koed, to: drop, by: skill, byOpponent: true)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is KO'd by an opponent's skill"

-- §21-14 — when this card KOs a card
DEFINE TRIGGER kos
  ON ko(role: cause)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card KOs a card"

-- §21-14 — when one of your cards is KO'd
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKoed
  ON ko(role: koed, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is KO'd"

-- Audit triggers 1 — "When one of your Battle Cards is KO'd by an opponent's
-- attack" (P-409): a battle's KO (8-4-6-2) of one of your cards, the card the
-- subject its description is asked of.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKoedByAttack
  ON ko(role: koed, by: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is KO'd by an attack"

-- §21-14 — when an opponent's card is KO'd
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardKoed
  ON ko(role: koed, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when an opponent's card is KO'd"

-- Phrasing batch 7 — "When a Battle Card that is in your opponent's Battle
-- Area and whose owner is your opponent is KO'd by your red card's attack or
-- skill" (BT28-001b): a KO one of your cards caused, by its attack or by its
-- skill — the `cause` role, which fires only for an opponent's card. The card
-- of yours that did it is the subject; what the text says of it ("red card")
-- is a condition on it.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKos
  ON ko(role: cause, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards KOs an opponent's card"

-- ── leaving a Battle Area (3-1, 9-6-9) ─────────────────────────────────────

-- Phrasing batch 7 — "When a <Pan> card or a card with <GT> in its character
-- name—both green and without <Son Goku: GT>—is placed from your Battle Area
-- in your Drop" (BT20-054b): another card of yours going from your Battle Area
-- to the Drop, by any cause (a KO, a skill, the rules) — `leftBattleToDrop`
-- said of another card. The card is the subject; its description a condition.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardBattleToDrop
  ON moved(from: battle, to: drop, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards goes from your Battle Area to the Drop"

-- §3-1-5 — when this card is removed from a Battle Area by a skill
DEFINE TRIGGER removedFromBattle
  ON moved(by: skill, from: battle)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is removed from a Battle Area by a skill"

-- §3-1-5 — when this card is removed from a Battle Area by an opponent's skill
DEFINE TRIGGER removedByOpponent
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: true, from: battle)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is removed from a Battle Area by an opponent's skill"

-- §3-1-5 — when a skill sends this card from a Battle Area to the Drop
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromBattle
  ON moved(by: skill, from: battle, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill sends this card from a Battle Area to the Drop"

-- §3-1-5 — the same move made by an opponent's skill: SD15-03's "placed in
-- your Drop Area from your Battle Area by an opponent's skill" (#728). Its
-- "or KO'd" half is `koed`; a KO is not a skill's move (`ko`, not `moved`).
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedByOpponent
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: true, from: battle, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when an opponent's skill sends this card from a Battle Area to the Drop"

-- §20-7 — when a skill sends this card from your hand to the Drop: a
-- discard by a skill's effect or as its cost (1-6, 1-7-1, 20-7-4). Pended by
-- name from a skill's own move, like `droppedFromBattle` above; a card leaving
-- the hand by the rules (an Extra after it is activated, 12-2-2) says no
-- `by: skill` and is not this.
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromHand
  ON moved(by: skill, from: hand, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill sends this card from your hand to the Drop"

-- §3-1-5 — when this card goes from a Battle Area to the Drop
DEFINE TRIGGER leftBattleToDrop
  ON moved(from: battle, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card goes from a Battle Area to the Drop"

-- BT29-029: "your Battle Area" is the original holder's, including a
-- borrowed card returning to its owner's hand (9-6-9-1-1/2).
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardReturnedToHand
  ON moved(from: battle, to: hand, watcher: fromHolder)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card is returned from your Battle Area to its owner's hand"

-- EX24-01b: "your Unison Area" is the original holder's, and the Unison is read
-- as it was when it left (the movement carries its information), whichever
-- area it went to.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourUnisonLeft
  ON moved(from: unison, watcher: fromHolder)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a Unison leaves your Unison Area"

-- Phrasing batch 5 — "When this card is placed in a Drop from Z-Energy or a
-- Battle Area" (BT23-092, P-563): the Z-Energy half, whatever the cause; the
-- Battle Area half is `leftBattleToDrop`.
DEFINE TRIGGER zEnergyToDrop
  ON moved(from: zEnergy, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card goes from your Z-Energy to the Drop"

-- Phrasing batch 5 — "When one of your red or blue Battle Cards is removed
-- from your Battle Area by an opponent's skill" (DB2-174, BT15-062, EX16-01):
-- `removedByOpponent` said of another card of yours, which is the subject.
-- Pended by name from a skill's own move, as that one is.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardRemovedByOpponent
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: true, from: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is removed from your Battle Area by an opponent's skill"

-- Phrasing batch 5 — "When your opponent's life is added to its owner's
-- Z-Energy by your skill" (BT23-103): a card of their Life Area moved to their
-- Z-Energy by a skill of yours. Pended by name from a skill's own move on the
-- cards of the skill's master, the moved card the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentLifeToZBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: true, from: life, to: zEnergy, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your skill adds your opponent's life to their Z-Energy"

-- Phrasing batch 5 — "When this card in your hand is discarded by one of your
-- skills" (BT26-015): `droppedFromHand` by a skill of the card's own master.
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromHandByYou
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: false, from: hand, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when one of your skills sends this card from your hand to the Drop"

-- Phrasing batch 5 — "When this card is sent from your Drop Area to your Warp
-- by a skill" (BT12-130, BT12-135): a skill's move, either player's. Pended by
-- name from a skill's own move, as `deckToWarpBySkill` is.
DEFINE TRIGGER dropToWarpBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, from: drop, to: warp)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill sends this card from your Drop to the Warp"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When this card is discarded from your hand by a [Union]
-- skill" (BT11-079, BT19-052), "…placed from a hand into its owner's Drop by a
-- [Union] skill" (P-683): a [Union] line's own move of it, its materials
-- (22-13-4-2) or its printed effect. Pended by name from a skill's own move,
-- which knows the line it runs (`union`).
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromHandByUnion
  ON moved(by: skill, from: hand, to: drop, union: true)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a [Union] skill sends this card from your hand to the Drop"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — the same move by a [Union-Fusion]: "…discarded from your
-- hand by a [Union-Fusion] skill" (P-246, P-247), "…placed in your Drop Area
-- from your hand as a result of [Union-Fusion]" (SD6-02, SD6-03, BT18-085).
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromHandByFusion
  ON moved(by: skill, from: hand, to: drop, union: Fusion)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a [Union-Fusion] skill sends this card from your hand to the Drop"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When a card in a Battle Area is returned to its owner's
-- hand by a skill" (BT12-029): either side's card, any skill (a card only
-- leaves a Battle Area for the hand by one). The returned card is the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER battleCardReturnedToHand
  ON moved(from: battle, to: hand, watcher: both)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card in a Battle Area is returned to its owner's hand"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When your energy is placed at the bottom of its owner's
-- deck" (BT30-030): a card of your Energy Area moved to the deck, any cause.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourEnergyToDeck
  ON moved(from: energy, to: deck, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your energy is placed in its owner's deck"

-- Audit triggers 1 — "When one of your blue Battle Cards is added to your
-- Z-Energy" (BT19-034's back), "…or one of your <Goku Black> is added to your
-- Z-Energy" (EX22-05): any card of yours, any cause; the description is a
-- condition on the card added.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardToZEnergy
  ON moved(to: zEnergy, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is added to your Z-Energy"

-- Audit triggers 1 — "When this card is placed in a Battle Area or removed
-- from the game" (BT27-094): its move to the removed area (20-10), heard there.
-- From an area only: a card under another card that moves answers to no
-- area-movement [Auto] (23-2-5-1; Q&A BT27-094, removed from under BT27-069),
-- and a pile card's move names no area it came from.
DEFINE TRIGGER removedFromGame
  ON moved(from: [deck, hand, drop, battle, combo, energy, life, warp, unison, zDeck, zEnergy], to: removed)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is removed from the game"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When one of your opponent's cards is added to their
-- Z-Energy" (BT21-038): any card of theirs, any cause.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardToZEnergy
  ON moved(to: zEnergy, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your opponent's cards is added to their Z-Energy"

-- BT3-112: Battle Area OR deck, and no restriction on the movement's cause.
DEFINE TRIGGER battleOrDeckToWarp
  ON moved(from: [battle, deck], to: warp)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card goes from your Battle Area or deck to the Warp"

-- §9-6-9-3 — when this card goes from a Battle Area to the Drop in Hidden
-- Mode. A card that moves face down answers to no other moment of its own
-- (`matchTriggers`); this is the "unless specified otherwise" (BT28-117).
DEFINE TRIGGER hiddenToDrop
  ON moved(from: battle, to: drop, hidden: true)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card goes from a Battle Area to the Drop in Hidden Mode"

-- ── damage and life (5-10, 3-9, 21-3) ──────────────────────────────────────

-- §5-10 — when this card deals damage. Phrasing batch 8 (owner's ruling of
-- 27 Oct 2026): by attacking or by its skill — the `damage` op pends it by
-- name with `by: skill` (`MOMENT_OF`), the battle fires it with `by: battle`.
DEFINE TRIGGER dealtDamage
  ON damage(role: source)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card deals damage"

-- Phrasing batch 8 — "When this card deals damage by attacking" (BT13-005),
-- "…deals damage to your opponent in a battle" (BT26-089): the battle's damage
-- only, never a skill's.
DEFINE TRIGGER dealtBattleDamage
  ON damage(role: source, by: battle)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card deals damage in a battle"

-- Phrasing batch 8 — "When you deal damage to your opponent by attacking with
-- a blue card" (BT30-017): the battle damage any of your cards deals, the
-- attacker the subject and its description a condition on it.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardDealtBattleDamage
  ON damage(role: source, by: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards deals damage by attacking"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When one of your cards deals damage to your opponent"
-- (BT9-104): the battle damage one of your cards deals, the attacker the
-- subject. Phrasing batch 7 (owner's ruling of 27 Oct 2026): a skill's damage
-- counts too — the `damage` op pends this by name for the cards in play of the
-- player whose card's skill dealt it, the skill's card the subject, as it
-- pends `dealtDamage`.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardDealtDamage
  ON damage(role: source, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards deals damage"

-- §21-3 — when you take damage from a skill
DEFINE TRIGGER youTookDamage
  ON damage(by: skill, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you take damage from a skill"

-- §21-3 — when your opponent takes damage from a skill
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentTookDamage
  ON damage(by: skill, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent takes damage from a skill"

-- Phrasing batch 10 (owner's ruling of 27 Oct 2026) — "When your opponent
-- takes damage from (non-keyword) skill(s) on (one of) your Battle Cards or
-- Unison Cards" (DB3-017, BT10-001b): a skill's damage whose skill's card sat
-- in its master's Battle or Unison Area. Since the same ruling, the other skill
-- damage moments are pended for any skill's damage, an Extra card's included;
-- the `damage` op pends this one by name only when the card is on the board.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentTookBoardSkillDamage
  ON damage(by: skill, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent takes damage from a skill on your Battle or Unison Cards"

-- Phrasing batch 9 (owner's ruling of 27 Oct 2026) — "When you take damage
-- from an opponent's non-keyword skill" (BT14-070): a skill's damage whose
-- skill is the opponent's. The `damage` op pends it by name only then, so
-- damage your own skill deals you is not this moment.
DEFINE TRIGGER youTookOpponentSkillDamage
  ON damage(by: skill, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you take damage from an opponent's skill"

-- Phrasing batch 8 — "When you take damage from an opponent's attack"
-- (BT21-071): the battle's damage, the attacker the subject. The battle's
-- `damage` moment is its attacker's master's, so the damaged player watches as
-- the opponent.
DEFINE TRIGGER youTookBattleDamage
  ON damage(by: battle, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you take damage from an opponent's attack"

-- §3-9 — when a card leaves your life
DEFINE TRIGGER lifeLeft
  ON moved(from: life, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card leaves your life"

-- §3-9-2-1 — when a card in your life is flipped face up
DEFINE TRIGGER flippedFaceUp
  ON faceUpTurned(in: life, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card in your life is flipped face up"

-- ── the turn (7-1 … 7-4) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- §7-2 — at the start of your Charge Phase
DEFINE TRIGGER chargeStart
  ON phaseStart(phase: charge)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: you)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of your Charge Phase"

-- §7-1 — at the start of your opponent's turn
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentTurnStart
  ON phaseStart(phase: charge)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: opponent)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of your opponent's turn"

-- §7-3 — at the start of your Main Phase
DEFINE TRIGGER mainStart
  ON phaseStart(phase: main)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: you)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of your Main Phase"

-- §7-3 — at the start of your opponent's Main Phase
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentMainStart
  ON phaseStart(phase: main)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: opponent)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the start of your opponent's Main Phase"

-- §7-3 — at the end of your Main Phase
DEFINE TRIGGER mainEnd
  ON phaseEnd(phase: main)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: you)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the end of your Main Phase"

-- §7-4 — at the end of your turn
DEFINE TRIGGER turnEnd
  ON phaseStart(phase: end)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: you)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the end of your turn"

-- §7-1 — at the end of your opponent's turn
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentTurnEnd
  ON phaseStart(phase: end)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: opponent)
  BIND "self"
  text: "at the end of your opponent's turn"

-- ── combos (5-7, 8-5-8) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- §8-5-6 — a Battle Area watcher of a same-player Combo-to-Drop departure.
-- Native cleanup announces this before 8-5-7 and suppresses only its repeat
-- at the physical 8-5-8 move. Other movement triggers still hear that move.
DEFINE TRIGGER comboToDrop
  ON moved(from: combo, to: drop, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card in your Combo Area is placed in your Drop Area"

-- §8-5-8 departure — ordinary self-combo wording already answered at entry;
-- the special "at battle end after combo" Auto is announced at 8-5-9.
DEFINE TRIGGER comboed
  ON moved(from: combo)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is used in a combo"

-- §§5-7-5-3/5-7-6-3 — this card's own Auto at Combo Area entry. `comboed`
-- remains the stored legacy alias and the distinct 8-5-10-1 cleanup moment.
DEFINE TRIGGER comboUsed
  ON comboUsed(to: combo)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when you combo with this card"

-- §5-7 — when you combo
DEFINE TRIGGER youCombo
  ON comboUsed(watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you combo"

-- §5-7 — when your opponent combos
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCombos
  ON comboUsed(watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent combos"

-- ── keyword activations (22) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

-- §22-4 — when this card activates [Blocker]
DEFINE TRIGGER blockerUsed
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Blocker)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card activates [Blocker]"

-- Phrasing batch 9 — "When your black card with a [Union] skill or black
-- Z-Unison attacks or activates the [Blocker] skill" (BT24-112 back): another
-- card of yours activating [Blocker], the blocker the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardBlockerUsed
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Blocker, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards activates [Blocker]"

-- §22-5-2-3/4 — successful evolution, distinct from keyword activation.
DEFINE TRIGGER evolvedInto
  ON evolved(to: battle)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card evolves into this card"

-- §22-5 — when you use this card's [Evolve] from your hand
DEFINE TRIGGER evolveFromHandActivated
  ON keywordActivated(from: hand, keyword: Evolve)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when you use this card's [Evolve] from your hand"

-- §22-13 — when you activate a [Union] skill
DEFINE TRIGGER unionActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Union, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate a [Union] skill"

-- §22-13-5 — when this card's [Union-Absorb] is activated
DEFINE TRIGGER unionAbsorbActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: "Union-Absorb")
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card's [Union-Absorb] is activated"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When you activate [Union-Fusion]" (BT10-092b): one of
-- your cards' [Union-Fusion], the [Union] card the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER unionFusionActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: "Union-Fusion", watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate a [Union-Fusion] skill"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When you activate [Union Absorb]" (BT30-044b), "When one
-- of your ≪Namekian≫ cards activates [Union Absorb]" (BT17-089): any of your
-- cards' [Union-Absorb], not only this card's (`unionAbsorbActivated`).
DEFINE TRIGGER unionAbsorbUsed
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: "Union-Absorb", watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate a [Union-Absorb] skill"

-- Phrasing batch 6 — "When you activate an [Evolve] or [Union] skill"
-- (BT14-094), "…[Evolve] or [Union Absorb]" (BT17-002b): any of your [Evolve]s.
DEFINE TRIGGER evolveActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Evolve, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate an [Evolve] skill"

-- §22-41 — when you activate an [Overlord] skill
DEFINE TRIGGER overlordActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Overlord, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate an [Overlord] skill"

-- §22-15 — when you play a card using [Over Realm]
DEFINE TRIGGER overRealmPlayed
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: "Over Realm", watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you play a card using [Over Realm]"

-- ── skills and counters (9-6, 9-7, 22-10) ──────────────────────────────────

-- §9-7 — when your opponent activates a [Counter] skill
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCounter
  ON skillActivated(kind: counter, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent activates a [Counter] skill"

-- Audit triggers 1 — "When your opponent activates a [Counter: Play] skill"
-- (EX13-19), "…a [Counter: Attack] skill": only that [Counter] (4-3), which the
-- activation says (`window`, the line's printed kind).
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCounterPlay
  ON skillActivated(kind: counter, window: play, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent activates a [Counter: Play] skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCounterAttack
  ON skillActivated(kind: counter, window: attack, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent activates a [Counter: Attack] skill"

-- §12-1-3 — when you activate an Extra Card from your hand. "Activating an
-- Extra Card" is using its [Activate] or [Counter] skill from the hand unless
-- the card says otherwise, [Field] included (22-3-1), so `from: hand` is the
-- whole of it; `extra: true` is the card's type, read before it went to the
-- Drop (12-2-2-2). The Extra is the subject, and what the card says about it
-- ("a blue Extra", BT29-029) is a condition on that subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER extraActivated
  ON skillActivated(extra: true, from: hand, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate an Extra Card from your hand"

-- §22-10 — when you activate this card's [Counter] from your hand without paying its energy cost
DEFINE TRIGGER counterFreeFromHand
  ON skillActivated(from: hand, kind: counter, paid: false)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when you activate this card's [Counter] from your hand without paying its energy cost"

-- ── modes and markers (1-10, 5-13, 22-32, 22-43) ───────────────────────────

-- §1-10-1 — when this card is rested by one of your skills
DEFINE TRIGGER restedBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, byOpponent: false, mode: rest)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is rested by one of your skills"

-- #907 — when this card is rested by a skill, whoever's: "by a skill"
-- (BT18-104, P-492). A keyword's own switch ([Alliance]) is its own moment
-- (`restedByAlliance`), so `by: skill` here, as above.
DEFINE TRIGGER restedByAnySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, mode: rest)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is rested by a skill"

-- #907 — when this card is rested by your opponent's skill. The moment carries
-- the skill's card, which a cause the card prints ("by your opponent's
-- <Name> card's skill") asks about as the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER restedByOpponentSkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, byOpponent: true, mode: rest)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is rested by your opponent's skill"

-- §1-10-1 — when your skill rests an opponent's card. The printed wording
-- names their Battle Cards and energy, which is where the legacy engine pends
-- it, and the skill is the other player's (#157).
DEFINE TRIGGER restedTheirsBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, byOpponent: true, in: [battle, energy], mode: rest, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your skill rests an opponent's card"

-- BT7-003 — an opponent's skill switches your energy. The text does not name
-- whose energy, so the matching SD8-09 form below covers their own energy
-- too. Charge Phase's ordinary Active switch carries no cause fields.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentEnergyActiveBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(byOpponent: true, notAwaken: true, in: energy, mode: active, watcher: controller)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent switches your energy to Active Mode using a non-[Awaken] skill during their turn"

-- SD8-09 — “their energy” narrows the switch to the opponent's energy.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentOwnEnergyActiveBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(byOpponent: false, notAwaken: true, in: energy, mode: active, watcher: opponent)
  WHERE isTurnPlayer(who: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent switches their energy to Active Mode using a non-[Awaken] skill during their turn"

-- #916 — "their energy" switched to Active by the opponent's own [Counter]
-- skill (DB3-013, -040, -059, -089, -105). The cause is the typed skill kind
-- the switching frame carries (`kind: counter`), not the source card's other
-- lines, and there is no turn restriction: a Counter is used on either turn.
-- The Charge Phase's rule-made switch carries no cause and never matches.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentOwnEnergyActiveByCounter
  ON modeSwitched(byOpponent: false, kind: counter, in: energy, mode: active, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent switches their energy to Active Mode using a [Counter] skill"

-- §1-10-1, §0-2-4-1 — when this card itself is switched from Rest Mode to Active
-- Mode (TB3-019, #922), by a skill or by the Charge Phase alike. A card already
-- Active does not switch, so no `modeSwitched` is fired for it. An arrival in
-- the Battle Area (a play, or the preliminary move of an energy-base [EX-Evolve],
-- 22-5-3-1-1) is a movement, never a mode switch, and does not match.
DEFINE TRIGGER selfRestToActive
  ON modeSwitched(mode: active, in: [battle, leader, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is switched from Rest Mode to Active Mode"

-- §1-10-2, §23-5-2-4 — when this card is switched to Hidden Mode by one of
-- your skills. The card is face down by the time it answers, and the pattern
-- naming `hidden: true` is what lets its front side do so (`matchTriggers`).
DEFINE TRIGGER hiddenBySkill
  ON hiddenSwitched(by: skill, byOpponent: false, hidden: true, in: battle)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is switched to Hidden Mode by one of your skills"

-- §1-10-2 — when this card is switched to Revealed Mode, whatever switched it.
-- In a Battle or Unison Area only: a card's skills are not valid in the
-- Energy Area (9-1-3-1), though its energy can be switched there.
DEFINE TRIGGER switchedRevealed
  ON hiddenSwitched(hidden: false, in: [battle, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is switched to Revealed Mode"

-- §1-10-2, §23-5-2-4 — when this card is switched to Hidden Mode, whatever
-- switched it; answered by its front side, as `hiddenBySkill` is.
DEFINE TRIGGER switchedHidden
  ON hiddenSwitched(hidden: true, in: [battle, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is switched to Hidden Mode"

-- §23-2 — when this card is placed under another card. The pile is a place
-- of its own, so the card answers there although its skills are not valid
-- under a card otherwise (23-2-2); the host is the card on top.
DEFINE TRIGGER placedUnder
  ON placedUnder(to: under)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is placed under a card"

-- §3-2, §3-3, §3-4 — when this card goes from your deck or hand to the Drop
DEFINE TRIGGER deckOrHandToDrop
  ON moved(from: [deck, hand], to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card goes from your deck or hand to the Drop"

-- §3-10 — when one of your skills sends this card from your deck to the Warp
-- (BT30-106). The skill's card is the subject the program is handed, so "by
-- your <Heles> card's skill" is a condition on it rather than a moment of its
-- own. Pended by name from a skill's `moveTo`, as `removedFromBattle` is.
DEFINE TRIGGER deckToWarpBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: false, from: deck, to: warp)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when one of your skills sends this card from your deck to the Warp"

-- §22-32-3 — when this card is rested by an [Alliance] skill
DEFINE TRIGGER restedByAlliance
  ON modeSwitched(by: Alliance, mode: rest)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is rested by an [Alliance] skill"

-- §5-13 — when a marker is removed from this card
DEFINE TRIGGER markerRemoved
  ON markerRemoved
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a marker is removed from this card"

-- §22-43-3 — when you pay a [Spirit Boost] cost from this card
DEFINE TRIGGER spiritBoostPaid
  ON markerRemoved(by: "Spirit Boost", watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you pay a [Spirit Boost] cost from this card"

-- ── areas outside play (3-8, 3-11, 3-13) ───────────────────────────────────

-- §3-8, §7-2-11 — when this card is placed in an Energy Area, from anywhere and
-- by anything: the Charge Phase's own placing (7-2-11) and a skill's alike
-- (BT18-052, EX17-02, "added to energy" P-617). Best guess, no official ruling
-- separates a charge from a skill's placing: both put a card in the Energy Area.
-- The card answers from there: the pattern names the place (9-1-3-1's exception).
DEFINE TRIGGER placedInEnergy
  ON moved(to: energy)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is placed in your energy"

-- #907 — the same arrival from the hand: "placed in your energy from your hand"
-- (BT13-040, -043, -045) and "this card in your hand is played or placed in
-- your energy" (EX19-26 …, P-353).
DEFINE TRIGGER placedInEnergyFromHand
  ON moved(from: hand, to: energy)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is placed in your energy from your hand"

-- §3-8 — when a card goes from your energy to the Drop
DEFINE TRIGGER energyToDrop
  ON moved(from: energy, to: drop, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when a card goes from your energy to the Drop"

-- §3-11-5 — when your Unison goes to the Drop
DEFINE TRIGGER unisonToDrop
  ON moved(from: unison, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when your Unison goes to the Drop"

-- §3-11, #930 — when this card is removed from a Unison Area: any move out of
-- it, whatever the cause (a skill, a new Unison replacing it 13-2-1-3, zero
-- markers 21-9-2) and wherever it goes (BT31-043).
DEFINE TRIGGER removedFromUnison
  ON moved(from: unison)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is removed from a Unison Area"

-- §3-13-1 — when this card is added to your Z-Energy
DEFINE TRIGGER addedToZEnergy
  ON moved(to: zEnergy)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is added to your Z-Energy"

-- ── moments batch 1 (2 Nov 2026) ───────────────────────────────────────────
-- The [Auto] moments of the triggerless list. Every one is pended by name by
-- the program step that causes it (`vm/host.ts`'s `MOMENT_OF`), never by a
-- native move: a skill's move from the hand, the deck, a pile, the energy or
-- a Battle Area, a power change (`power`) and a pile left. A self-moment hands
-- the skill's card on as the subject, so the cause a card prints ("by your
-- Leader's skill", "by a <Dr. Hedo: SH> card skill") is a condition on it.

-- §20-7-1 — when an opponent's skill discards this card (BT13-098)
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromHandByOpponent
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: true, from: hand, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when an opponent's skill sends this card from your hand to the Drop"

-- §1-10-1 — when a skill switches this card to Active Mode (BT22-019). The
-- switch carries the skill's card (`modeSwitched`'s source), the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER activeBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, mode: active, in: [battle, leader, unison])
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is switched to Active Mode by a skill"

-- §1-10-1 — when a skill switches your energy to Active Mode (BT22-137), once
-- per energy card switched
DEFINE TRIGGER yourEnergyActiveBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, in: energy, mode: active, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your energy is switched to Active Mode by a skill"

-- Power changed by a skill's effect (`power` op, 5-6): once per card and per
-- change (BT9-002's Q&A: -10000 and -5000 are two moments).
DEFINE TRIGGER powerRaisedBySkill
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, dir: up)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card's power is increased by a skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER powerLoweredBySkill
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, dir: down)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card's power is decreased by a skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPowerRaisedByYou
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, byOpponent: false, dir: up, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your skills increases the power of one of your cards"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPowerLowered
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, dir: down, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when the power of one of your cards is decreased"

DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardPowerLowered
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, dir: down, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when the power of one of your opponent's cards is decreased"

-- §20-1-2: "by the skill of one of your Battle Cards" — a Battle Card in your
-- Battle Area (BT9-002's Q&A), pended only then.
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardPowerLoweredByBattleCard
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, byOpponent: true, dir: down, fromBattleCard: true, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when the skill of one of your Battle Cards decreases the power of an opponent's card"

DEFINE TRIGGER eitherCardPowerLowered
  ON powerChanged(by: skill, dir: down, watcher: both)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when the power of a card of either player is decreased"

-- A skill's move out of the deck into the Drop (BT16-009, SD16-02), and the
-- card a skill revealed from the top of the deck and placed there (BT14-095).
DEFINE TRIGGER deckToDropBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, from: deck, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill places this card from your deck in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER deckToDropByYou
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: false, from: deck, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when one of your skills places this card from your deck in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER revealedTopToDrop
  ON moved(by: skill, from: deck, revealed: true, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card is revealed from the top of your deck and placed in the Drop"

-- §23-2: a pile is in no area, so its moments are its host's (`pileLeft`)
-- and the card's own move out of it (`fromPile: true`).
DEFINE TRIGGER underReturnedToHand
  ON pileLeft(to: hand)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a card under this card is returned to its owner's hand"

DEFINE TRIGGER underToDropBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, fromPile: true, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill places this card from under a card in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER underLeaderToDropBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, fromPile: leader, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill places this card from under a Leader in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER pileToDropBySkill
  ON pileLeft(by: skill, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill places a card from under this card in the Drop"

-- A skill's move out of the Energy Area into the Drop (EB1-16, EX22-03).
DEFINE TRIGGER energyToDropBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, from: energy, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill places this card from your energy in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourEnergyToDropByYourLeader
  ON moved(by: skill, byLeader: true, byOpponent: false, from: energy, to: drop, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your Leader's skill places one of your energy in the Drop"

-- Audit conditions 2 review: "When a card in your energy is placed in your Drop Area by one of your skills" (XD2-01's
-- back, XD2-04) — any skill of yours, never the opponent's; pended by name as the Leader's one is (`yourSkill` is
-- the name's own mark, so a plain move that says `by: skill` is not answered twice).
DEFINE TRIGGER yourEnergyToDropByYou
  ON moved(by: skill, yourSkill: true, byOpponent: false, from: energy, to: drop, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your skills places one of your energy in the Drop"

-- §3-1: "by one of your skills" from a Battle Area (BT18-023), and the Drop
-- reached from any area by a skill (P-421), yours (P-701), theirs (BT30-058).
-- A skill's KO is a move to the Drop too (5-12-1): its native move carries the
-- cause (`flow.ts`), so these answer it without a name.
DEFINE TRIGGER droppedFromBattleByYou
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: false, from: battle, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when one of your skills sends this card from a Battle Area to the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER toDropBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when a skill places this card in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER toDropByYou
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: false, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when one of your skills places this card in the Drop"

DEFINE TRIGGER toDropByOpponent
  ON moved(by: skill, byOpponent: true, to: drop)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when an opponent's skill places this card in the Drop"

-- ── audit triggers 2 (3 Nov 2026): the watched-card moment grammar ─────────
-- One sentence shape — whose card × what happened to it × who caused it — read
-- by one grammar (`watchedMomentOf`, text/triggers.ts), each pair naming one of
-- these. The card the moment is about is the subject, and what the sentence
-- says about it is a condition on it, asked before pending (9-6-2).

-- §3-1 — "When one of your ≪Red Ribbon Army≫ cards is removed from your Battle
-- Area by a skill" (BT17-038), any skill's; the opponent's side of it (DB3-103).
-- Pended by name from a skill's move (`moveTo`), about the card moved.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardRemovedBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, from: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is removed from a Battle Area by a skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardRemovedBySkill
  ON moved(by: skill, from: battle, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your opponent's cards is removed from a Battle Area by a skill"

-- §5-12 — a KO told by its cause, watched: "When one of your green Battle
-- Cards is KO'd by an opponent's skill" (BT15-072), "…by one of your skills"
-- (BT25-077), "When an opponent's Battle Card is KO'd by one of your skills"
-- (BT24-008), "…KO'd by your opponent" (TB3-035: their attack or their skill).
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKoedByOpponentSkill
  ON ko(role: koed, by: skill, byOpponent: true, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is KO'd by an opponent's skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKoedByYourSkill
  ON ko(role: koed, by: skill, byOpponent: false, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is KO'd by one of your skills"

DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardKoedByYourSkill
  ON ko(role: koed, by: skill, byOpponent: true, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your opponent's cards is KO'd by one of your skills"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKoedByOpponent
  ON ko(role: koed, byOpponent: true, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is KO'd by your opponent"

-- §8-4-6-2 — "When one of your green Battle Cards attacks and KOs an
-- opponent's Battle Card" (BT16-050): the battle's KO, the attacker the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardKosByAttack
  ON ko(role: cause, by: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards attacks and KOs an opponent's Battle Card"

-- §8-1-3 — "When one of your cards is attacked" (BT13-023), "When a ≪Universe
-- 7≫ <Son Goku> card in your Battle Area is attacked" (SD21-03).
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardAttacked
  ON attackDeclared(role: target, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is attacked"

-- §13-2 — "When one of your green Unison Cards is placed in your Drop Area"
-- (BT17-069): from your Unison Area, never one discarded from the hand (its
-- Q&A, and BT17-059's).
DEFINE TRIGGER yourUnisonToDrop
  ON moved(from: unison, to: drop, watcher: fromHolder)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your Unison Cards is placed in your Drop Area from your Unison Area"

-- §3-1-5 — "When your Battle Card is removed from a Battle Area" (BT27-059),
-- "When your {Power-Infused Shocking Death Ball} leaves the Battle Area"
-- (BT26-030): no cause named, so any departure — a KO, a skill's move, a
-- combo from the Battle Area (BT28-066's Q&A). The side asked is the moved
-- card's (`controller`): a skill's move by name carries no original holder.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardLeftBattle
  ON moved(from: battle, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards leaves a Battle Area"

-- §5-5 — one of your cards played from a place the sentence names: "When a
-- black Battle Card is played from your Warp" (BT16-110), "When a blue card is
-- played from your energy" (BT17-032b), "When you play a Battle Card from your
-- life" (P-406); `yourCardPlayedFromHand`/`…FromDrop` are the other two.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPlayedFromWarp
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: warp, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is played from your Warp"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPlayedFromEnergy
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: energy, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is played from your Energy Area"

DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardPlayedFromLife
  ON moved(asPlay: true, from: life, to: [battle, unison], watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards is played from your Life Area"

-- §1-10 — a Battle Card (20-1-2: in a Battle Area) switched to Rest Mode by any
-- skill, watched: "When one of your yellow ≪Android≫ Battle Cards is switched
-- to Rest Mode by a skill" (BT13-092), "When one of your opponent's Battle Cards
-- is switched to Rest Mode by a skill" (DB1-075). `opponentCardRestedByYourSkill`
-- below is the switch of any card of theirs by your skill.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourBattleCardRestedBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, in: battle, mode: rest, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your Battle Cards is switched to Rest Mode by a skill"

DEFINE TRIGGER opponentBattleCardRestedBySkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, in: battle, mode: rest, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your opponent's Battle Cards is switched to Rest Mode by a skill"

-- §1-10 — "When an opponent's card is switched to Rest Mode by one of your
-- skills" (BT10-139, BT19-148, EX06-22), "When one of your opponent's cards is
-- …" (BT12-105, DB2-108), "…by your skill" (BT8-075): any card of theirs on the
-- table — their Leader too, which "your opponent's cards" chooses (20-1-6), a
-- Unison, and energy (R-208, pending: the legacy engine's reading of the
-- sentence named energy). `restedTheirsBySkill` keeps XD1-01's narrower
-- "an opponent's Battle Card or energy".
DEFINE TRIGGER opponentCardRestedByYourSkill
  ON modeSwitched(by: skill, byOpponent: true, in: [leader, battle, unison, energy], mode: rest, watcher: opponent)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your opponent's cards is switched to Rest Mode by one of your skills"

-- §22-5 — "When a yellow Battle Card activates an [EX-Evolve] skill from your
-- hand" (BT16-073): the move's own moment, from the hand, the evolving card the
-- subject. `evolveActivated` is any [Evolve] of yours.
DEFINE TRIGGER yourCardExEvolveFromHand
  ON keywordActivated(from: hand, keyword: "EX-Evolve", watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when one of your cards activates [EX-Evolve] from your hand"

-- §22-22 — "When you activate [Swap]" (BT28-086), "When one of your red Battle
-- Cards activates a [Swap] skill" (BT11-004): the move's own moment, the card
-- that returns to the hand the subject.
DEFINE TRIGGER swapActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Swap, watcher: controller)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when you activate a [Swap] skill"

-- §22-30 — "When this card activates [Aegis]" (EX05-03), "…activates its [Aegis
-- Blue/Yellow] skill" (BT16-130): the move's own moment, on the card itself.
DEFINE TRIGGER aegisActivated
  ON keywordActivated(keyword: Aegis)
  BIND "self"
  text: "when this card activates [Aegis]"

-- ── the counter windows (4-3, 9-7) ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- A [Counter] answers to a window rather than to a card's moment, so these
-- five carry a name a card's WHEN never says. The shape is the same: the
-- moment as the event that is it.

-- §9-6-6 — the window after a card is played and before it resolves
DEFINE TRIGGER "counter:play"
  ON counterTiming(watcher: opponent, window: play)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent plays a card, before it resolves"

-- §8-1-4 — the window after an attack is declared
DEFINE TRIGGER "counter:attack"
  ON counterTiming(watcher: opponent, window: attack)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent declares an attack"

-- §8-1-4 — the same window, narrowed to an attack a Battle Card made
DEFINE TRIGGER "counter:battleCardAttack"
  ON counterTiming(attacker: battleCard, watcher: opponent, window: attack)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent's Battle Card declares an attack"

-- §9-7-4 — the window after a [Counter] skill is activated
DEFINE TRIGGER "counter:counter"
  ON counterTiming(watcher: opponent, window: counter)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent activates a [Counter] skill, before it resolves"

-- §9-6-6 — the window after a skill is activated
DEFINE TRIGGER "counter:skill"
  ON counterTiming(watcher: opponent, window: skill)
  BIND "subject"
  text: "when your opponent activates a skill, before it resolves"
